In article <Qa8=fOa00WY7E_tEQD@andrew.cmu.edu> ms7i+@andrew.cmu.edu (Michael Harlan Shea) writes:
>Okay, so I #dip a piece of armor into my holy water, and everything goes
>just great, until I notice my water is gone.
>
>How do I prevent this from happening?
>
>-Mike Shea

Make more holy water.  Pick up potions.  Dilute useless potions by dipping
them twice in a fountain.  Collect many potions of water under the same
directory entry by dropping them in one place and picking them up all at
the same time.  With, say, 10 potions of water under the same inventory
entry (like, a) 10 potions of water), dip them into the holy water thus
creating 10 blessed potions.  Should last a while.  There might be a better
way, but this is just my 0.02$.  All I can afford...

